Package: linexinbar
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Piotr Lewandowski <piotr.petexiness@gmail.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, dbus, libwayland-client0, libwayland-server0,
 libwayland-egl1, libegl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcb1, libxcursor1,
 libxi6, libxkbcommon-x11-0
Recommends: seatd, xwayland, libgl1-mesa-dri, wireplumber,
 pulseaudio-utils, hicolor-icon-theme, sudo, pipewire, xdg-desktop-portal
Suggests: alsa-utils, ddcutil, mesa-vulkan-drivers
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/petexy/project-linexinbar
Description: multi-display Wayland desktop with an XMB-style shell
 LineXinBar combines a small DRM/KMS Wayland compositor with a GPU-rendered,
 gamepad-friendly desktop shell. Every connected display is managed as an
 independent output.
 .
 This early-development package includes the compositor, shell, desktop portal,
 bundled cursor theme and a display-manager Wayland session.
